ded and there is no related order. object.order.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedOrderSummaryInput}. An order's summary fields, including status, payment and refund status, and pricing and settlement amounts, returned when the order is expanded. object.order.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.order_id (Optional): string. ID of the order the disputed payment was for. Absent when Flint can't link the dispute to an order. Example: "ord_01KEZF7C0054GQKJ142A8X367A". object.payment_intent (Optional): {@see ExpandedPaymentIntentSummaryInput} or null. Present only when `expand` includes `payment_intent`; `null` when expanded and there is no related payment intent. object.payment_intent.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedPaymentIntentSummaryInput}. A payment intent's summary fields, including amount, status, and capture method, returned when the payment intent is expanded. object.payment_intent.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.payment_intent_id (Optional): string. ID of the payment intent that took the disputed payment. Absent when Flint can't link the dispute to a payment intent. Example: "pi_01KEZF7C00G8H9D509YEV22P7R". object.payment_option (Required): string or null. How the buyer paid for the disputed payment. `null` when Flint hasn't linked the dispute to a payment intent that records a payment option. Value enum: "card", "apple_pay", "google_pay", "affirm", "ach_debit", null. object.reason (Required): string. Why the payment was disputed. A reason Flint doesn't recognize is `other`. Value enum: "fraudulent", "unrecognized", "duplicate", "product_not_received", "product_not_as_described", "refund_not_processed", "subscription_canceled", "noncompliant", "insufficient_funds", "debit_not_authorized", "bank_account_not_found", "other". object.recommended_evidence_types (Required): Array of string. Evidence types that usually answer this reason, chosen by Flint, most useful first. Use the ones that fit what you sold. Empty when Flint has no recommendation, including bank returns. Chosen from the stored reason and case_type; in a webhook, frozen when Flint records the change. [] enum: "customer_details", "customer_communication", "customer_signature", "receipt", "shipping_documentation", "service_documentation", "access_activity_log", "product_description", "refund_policy", "duplicate_charge_documentation", "cancellation_policy". object.recommended_evidence_types[] (Value): string.  Value enum: "customer_details", "customer_communication", "customer_signature", "receipt", "shipping_documentation", "service_documentation", "access_activity_log", "product_description", "refund_policy", "duplicate_charge_documentation", "cancellation_policy". object.response_unavailable_reason (Optional): string. Why a response is unavailable when can_respond_with_evidence is false. Absent when no reason is reported. Current values are bank_return_not_contestable and response_window_unavailable. response_window_unavailable means no evidence deadline was supplied. Value enum: "bank_return_not_contestable", "response_window_unavailable". object.split_reversals (Optional): Array of {@see SplitReversalReferenceInput}. Fixed seller allocations on the payment, each naming its payment split and reversal. Present only when the payment has splits; an empty array means no seller share was allocated. Read PaymentSplit.reversals for status, shortfall, and reinstated amounts. object.split_reversals[] (Value): {@see SplitReversalReferenceInput}. A fixed allocation referencing a read-only reversal nested in a payment split. This reference has no independent lifecycle or write routes. object.status (Required): string. Where the dispute stands. `needs_response` and `inquiry_needs_response` ask you to respond; `inquiry_closed`, `won`, `lost`, and `prevented` are final. Value enum: "inquiry_needs_response", "inquiry_under_review", "inquiry_closed", "needs_response", "under_review", "won", "lost", "prevented", "other". object.status_changed_at (Optional): string. Recorded time of the 